# Laravel Conventions

## Controllers
- Use FormRequest classes for validation, never validate inline.
- One resource = one controller. Don't mix concerns.
- Return type: `RedirectResponse`, `View`, `JsonResponse`.

```php
// GOOD
public function update(UpdateOrderRequest $request, SourcingOrder $order, OrderService $service): RedirectResponse
{
    $service->update($order, $request->validated());
    return back()->with('success', __('Order updated.'));
}
```

## Services
- Constructor injection for dependencies.
- Return typed values, throw exceptions on failure.
- Never return HTTP responses from services.

## Repositories
- One repository per aggregate root model.
- Return models or collections, never arrays.
- All complex queries (filters, search, joins) belong here.

## Eloquent
- Always eager load relationships: `->with(['user', 'quotation'])`.
- Use `$model->load()` when model already loaded.
- Never use `DB::` facade in application code (use Eloquent).
- Use database transactions for multi-model operations.

## Notifications & Queue
- All notifications implement `ShouldQueue`.
- Set `$tries = 3`, `$maxExceptions = 3`, `$backoff = [60, 300, 900]`.
- Call `$this->afterCommit()` in constructor.
- Never use `retryUntil()` with long durations.

## Naming
- Services: `OrderStatusService`, `RefundService`
- Repositories: `EloquentSourcingOrderRepository`
- FormRequests: `StoreQuotationRequest`, `UpdateTrackingRequest`
- Events: past tense (`QuotationAccepted`, `OrderStatusChanged`)
- Listeners: imperative (`SendQuotationNotification`, `InitializeFsbTracking`)

## Translations
- All user-facing strings must use `__()` or `@lang()`.
- Add keys to both `lang/en.json` and `lang/fr.json`.
